(6784895, 1017278, 146356, '<td valign="top">So, I''ve got a question for ya.<br/> <br/>I know you had fire to cover the topside of the wings, but in a scenario where you don''t - how do you go about creating the right texture of the topside of the wings. Would you just leave the curved distorted feather shapes as is or would you smooth them out further to create a "thickness"?<br/> <br/></td>', 'So, I''ve got a question for ya. I know you had fire to cover the topside of the wings, but in a scenario where you don''t - how do you go about creating the right texture of the topside of the wings. Would you just leave the curved distorted feather shapes as is or would you smooth them out further to create a "thickness"? ', '2012-06-03 19:58:22.000000', NULL, 0),
